<section class="card" id="android" style="margin-top: 16px;">
  <h3 class="section-title">Android (Private DNS)</h3>
  <p>Android 9 and later supports DNS-over-TLS natively, system-wide.</p>
  <ol class="steps">
    <li>Open <strong>Settings</strong> → <strong>Network &amp; Internet</strong> → <strong>Private DNS</strong>.</li>
    <li>Choose <strong>Private DNS provider hostname</strong>.</li>
    <li>Enter: <strong>{{ site.endpoints.dotHost }}</strong></li>
    <li>Save. Confirm on the <a href="#verify">verification widget</a>.</li>
  </ol>
  <div class="code-block" style="margin-top: 10px;"><span class="lang">android</span><span class="cmt"># Settings path</span>
Settings → Network &amp; Internet → Private DNS
Mode: <span class="hl">Private DNS provider hostname</span>
Hostname: <span class="hl-purple">{{ site.endpoints.dotHost }}</span></div>
  <p class="mini">Some carriers prevent Private DNS from being used on cellular. Wi-Fi networks should always work.</p>
</section>

<section class="card" id="ios" style="margin-top: 16px;">
  <h3 class="section-title">iPhone and iPad (encrypted DNS profile)</h3>
  <p>iOS uses a configuration profile to set the encrypted resolver system-wide. The AEGIS profile uses DNS-over-HTTPS.</p>
  <ol class="steps">
    <li>From Safari on the device, open <a href="/aegis.mobileconfig">/aegis.mobileconfig</a> (other browsers won't install profiles).</li>
    <li>iOS prompts you to allow the download. Open <strong>Settings</strong>, you'll see a banner saying <em>Profile Downloaded</em>.</li>
    <li>Tap the banner → <strong>Install</strong> → enter your passcode → <strong>Install</strong> again.</li>
    <li>Verify in <strong>Settings</strong> → <strong>General</strong> → <strong>VPN &amp; Device Management</strong>.</li>
  </ol>

  <div class="shot-row">
    <a href="#" data-lightbox="/assets/img/setup/ios/page01_img01.png" data-caption="Safari prompts to allow the profile download.">
      <img class="shot" src="/assets/img/setup/ios/page01_img01.png" alt="Safari profile download prompt" />
    </a>
    <a href="#" data-lightbox="/assets/img/setup/ios/page02_img01.png" data-caption="Profile Downloaded banner in Settings.">
      <img class="shot" src="/assets/img/setup/ios/page02_img01.png" alt="iOS Profile Downloaded banner" />
    </a>
    <a href="#" data-lightbox="/assets/img/setup/ios/page02_img02.png" data-caption="Install confirmation in Settings.">
      <img class="shot" src="/assets/img/setup/ios/page02_img02.png" alt="iOS profile install confirm" />
    </a>
    <a href="#" data-lightbox="/assets/img/setup/ios/page02_img03.png" data-caption="Profile installed.">
      <img class="shot" src="/assets/img/setup/ios/page02_img03.png" alt="iOS profile installed" />
    </a>
    <a href="#" data-lightbox="/assets/img/setup/ios/page03_img01.png" data-caption="VPN & Device Management view.">
      <img class="shot" src="/assets/img/setup/ios/page03_img01.png" alt="iOS VPN and Device Management" />
    </a>
  </div>

  <div class="btnrow" style="margin-top: 12px;">
    <a class="btn primary" href="/aegis.mobileconfig">Download AEGIS DNS profile</a>
  </div>

  <p class="mini" id="downloadProfile" style="margin-top: 12px;">
    Prefer manual configuration? In <strong>Settings</strong> → <strong>General</strong> → <strong>VPN, DNS &amp; Device Management</strong>, choose <strong>DNS</strong> and enter the DoT hostname: <strong>{{ site.endpoints.dotHost }}</strong>.
  </p>
  <div class="code-block" style="margin-top: 10px;"><span class="lang">ios</span><span class="cmt"># Manual DoT configuration (no profile)</span>
Settings → General → VPN, DNS &amp; Device Management → DNS
Server type: <span class="hl">Encrypted DNS (DoT)</span>
Hostname: <span class="hl-purple">{{ site.endpoints.dotHost }}</span></div>
</section>

<section class="card" id="routers" style="margin-top: 16px;">
  <h3 class="section-title">Routers</h3>
  <p>If your router supports encrypted DNS, set it once and every device on the network is covered.</p>
  <ul class="list">
    <li>DoT upstream: <strong>{{ site.endpoints.dotHost }}</strong>, port <strong>{{ site.endpoints.dotPort }}</strong></li>
    <li>DoH upstream: <strong>{{ site.endpoints.doh }}</strong></li>
    <li>If your firmware exposes DoQ, point it to <strong>{{ site.endpoints.doqHost }}</strong> on port <strong>{{ site.endpoints.doqPort }}</strong>.</li>
  </ul>

  <div class="code-block" style="margin-top: 10px;"><span class="lang">openwrt</span><span class="cmt"># /etc/config/dhcp: point dnsmasq upstream at AEGIS DoT via stubby/unbound</span>
config server
  option address <span class="hl-purple">'/#/{{ site.endpoints.dotHost }}'</span>
  option port    <span class="hl-purple">'{{ site.endpoints.dotPort }}'</span>
  option proto   <span class="hl">'tls'</span></div>

  <div class="code-block" style="margin-top: 10px;"><span class="lang">systemd-resolved</span><span class="cmt"># /etc/systemd/resolved.conf.d/aegis.conf</span>
[Resolve]
DNS=<span class="hl-purple">{{ site.endpoints.dotHost }}#{{ site.endpoints.dotHost }}</span>
DNSOverTLS=<span class="hl">yes</span>
DNSSEC=allow-downgrade</div>

  <p class="mini">OpenWrt, Ubiquiti EdgeOS, MikroTik, AsusWRT-Merlin, and pfSense / OPNsense all support at least DoT.</p>
</section>

<section class="card" id="browsers" style="margin-top: 16px;">
  <h3 class="section-title">Browsers</h3>
  <p>Browser-level DNS-over-HTTPS only protects that browser's traffic. Other apps still use the system resolver.</p>
  <ol class="steps">
    <li>Open your browser's privacy settings.</li>
    <li>Find the <strong>DNS over HTTPS</strong> section.</li>
    <li>Choose <strong>Custom</strong> and paste:</li>
  </ol>
  <div class="code-block" style="margin-top: 10px;"><span class="lang">browser</span><span class="cmt"># Firefox: about:preferences#privacy → Enable DNS over HTTPS</span>
<span class="cmt"># Chrome:  chrome://settings/security  → Use secure DNS → Custom</span>
DoH URL: <span class="hl-purple">{{ site.endpoints.doh }}</span></div>
</section>

<section class="card" id="verify" style="margin-top: 16px;">
  <h3 class="section-title">Live verification</h3>
  <p>The verification runs directly from your browser against the selected resolver. No separate backend service is used for this test page, but DNS queries are sent to the resolver endpoint being tested.</p>

  <div class="endpoint">
    <div class="label">
      <span>DoH endpoint under test</span>
      <span class="badge">read-only</span>
    </div>
    <div class="mono" id="verifyDohUrl">{{ site.endpoints.doh }}</div>
    <div class="mono" id="blockHost" style="margin-top: 6px;">{{ site.endpoints.blockTestHost }}</div>
  </div>

  <div class="statusline">
    <span class="pill"><span class="led" id="vLed"></span><span id="vStatus">Idle</span></span>
  </div>

  <div class="btnrow">
    <button class="btn primary" type="button" onclick="verifyAll()">Run all checks</button>
    <button class="btn" type="button" onclick="verifyReachability()">Reachability</button>
    <button class="btn" type="button" onclick="verifyBinaryExample()">DoH query (allow-test canary)</button>
    <button class="btn" type="button" onclick="verifyBlockTest()">Block test</button>
    <button class="btn purple" type="button" onclick="verifyBinaryExample('google.com')" title="Optional external sanity check: confirms the resolver can resolve a well-known external domain.">External sanity (google.com)</button>
    <button class="btn" type="button" onclick="clearVerify()">Reset</button>
  </div>

  <div class="grid3" style="margin-top: 16px;">
    <div class="tile">
      <h3>Reachability</h3>
      <p><strong id="rReach">Not run</strong></p>
      <p class="mini" id="dReach"></p>
    </div>
    <div class="tile">
      <h3>DoH query</h3>
      <p><strong id="rBin">Not run</strong></p>
      <p class="mini" id="dBin"></p>
      <p class="mini" id="dBinExtra"></p>
    </div>
    <div class="tile">
      <h3>Block test</h3>
      <p><strong id="rBlock">Not run</strong></p>
      <p class="mini" id="dBlock"></p>
      <p class="mini" id="dBlockExtra"></p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p class="mini" id="vSummary" style="margin-top: 10px;"></p>
</section>
